    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d179-a1">

                <pb facs="0298" n="228" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg228"/>

                <head>Mr. Welles to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy Department,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-10-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 29, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy of a communication received from Rear Admiral Charles Wilkes, commanding
                    the West India squadron, reporting the infraction of the neutrality regulations
                    by the commander of her Britannic Majesty’s gunboat Bull Dog, in transporting
                    officers from Nassau to Bermuda, in July last, on their way to England to take
                    charge of vessels about to fit out there under the rebel flag.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GIDEON WELLES, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                        Navy.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d179-a1-a1.xml" xpointer="d179-a1-a1"/>
